  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you don't have a commander, Arcane Signet's ability produces no mana.",
      "oracle_id": "0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you have two commanders, the ability adds one mana of any color in their combined color identities.",
      "oracle_id": "0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your commander is a card that has no colors in its color identity, Arcane Signet's ability produces no mana. It doesn't produce {C}.",
      "oracle_id": "0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although Urza's Saga has the Urza's land type, it doesn't interact with Urza's Tower, Urza's Mine, or Urza's Power Plant.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Even though Urza's Saga is a land, it is also still a Saga, and it will be sacrificed after its last chapter ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Urza's Saga loses all of its chapter abilities but is still a Saga, perhaps due to a card like Blood Moon, it will immediately be sacrificed.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Urza's Saga gains an ability from its first and second chapters. It keeps those abilities for as long as it's on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Urza's Saga is a land, so it can only be played as a land. It cannot be cast as a spell.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While resolving the chapter III ability, you can find only a card with actual mana cost {0} or {1}, not mana value 0 or 1. For example, you couldn't find a card with mana cost {U} or one with mana cost {X}.",
      "oracle_id": "4c6a0c30-b547-4eff-8ff4-0ca25803c076",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Colorless mana won't give Engineered Explosives another charge counter. Colorless is not a color.",
      "oracle_id": "95fd897e-9086-42c4-8e0d-61bb02333c5f",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.",
      "oracle_id": "95fd897e-9086-42c4-8e0d-61bb02333c5f",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens that aren't a copy of something else don't have a mana cost. Anything without a mana cost normally has a mana value of 0.",
      "oracle_id": "95fd897e-9086-42c4-8e0d-61bb02333c5f",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can choose any value for X as you cast Engineered Explosives. The value chosen for X doesn't directly affect the number of charge counters Engineered Explosives enters the battlefield with, but it does let you pay more mana and thus spend more colors of mana to cast it.",
      "oracle_id": "95fd897e-9086-42c4-8e0d-61bb02333c5f",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ]
